=== What the rules allow ===
  borrow twice (two readers)                   -> ok, 'hello'
  move, then use the NEW owner                 -> ok, 'world'

=== What the rules reject ===
  use after move                               -> REJECTED: use after move
  mutable borrow while shared                  -> REJECTED: cannot mutably borrow while already borrowed
  second mutable borrow                        -> REJECTED: cannot mutably borrow while already borrowed
  move while borrowed                          -> REJECTED: cannot move while borrowed

Rust does all four of these checks at COMPILE time, so none of
these programs would ever run. Here they raise at run time, which
is precisely the binding-time difference the theory section names.
